{:edb/committed true :edb/basis-t 1093 :edb/replayed false :edb/tx-hash "bfb693ada4c2c23356440b8a92aa8842127a651ec426de32c9a3648a2545dd7b" :edb/db-before-t 1092 :edb/db-after-t 1093 :edb/tx-data [[13194139534405 50 #inst "2026-10-07T00:44:27.569Z" 13194139534405 true] [17592186114946 1100 "Calculate $\\displaystyle \\int_{-1}^{2} 9 x^2 \\, \\textrm d x .$" 13194139534405 true] [17592186114946 1100 "Calculate $\\displaystyle \\int_{-1}^{2} 9 x^2 \\, \\textrm d x$." 13194139534405 false] [17592186114946 1145 "Factoring the constant out of the integral, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\int_{-1}^{2}9x^{2}dx &= 9\\int_{-1}^{2}x^{2}dx \\\\\n&= 9 \\cdot \\left.\\frac{x^{3}}{3}\\right|_{-1}^{2} \\\\\n&= \\left.3x^{3}\\right|_{-1}^{2} \\\\\n&= 3(2^{3} - (-1)^{3}) \\\\\n&= 3(8 - (-1)) \\\\\n&= 3 \\cdot 9 \\\\\n&= 27\n\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534405 false] [17592186114946 1145 "Factoring the constant out of the integral, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{-1}^{2}9{x}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x & =9{\\int }_{-1}^{2}{x}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =9\\cdot \\frac{{x}^{3}}{3}\\,{|}_{-1}^{2} \\\\  & =3{x}^{3}\\,{|}_{-1}^{2} \\\\  & =3({2}^{3}-(-1)^{3}) \\\\  & =3(8-(-1)) \\\\  & =3\\cdot 9 \\\\  & =27.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534405 true] [17592186114953 1100 "Evaluate $\\displaystyle \\int_{0}^{\\pi/4} (\\sec x \\tan x - \\cos x)\\, \\textrm d x$." 13194139534405 false] [17592186114953 1100 "Evaluate $\\displaystyle \\int_{0}^{\\pi/4} (\\sec x \\tan x - \\cos x)\\, \\textrm d x.$" 13194139534405 true] [17592186114953 1145 "Splitting up the integral into the difference of two integrals and evaluating each integral separately, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\int_{0}^{π/4}(\\sec x\\tan x - \\cos x)dx &= \\int_{0}^{π/4}\\sec x\\tan xdx - \\int_{0}^{π/4}\\cos xdx \\\\\n&= \\left.\\sec x\\right|_{0}^{π/4} - \\left.\\sin x\\right|_{0}^{π/4} \\\\\n&= (\\sec \\frac{π}{4} - \\sec 0) - (\\sin \\frac{π}{4} - \\sin 0) \\\\\n&= (\\sqrt{2} - 1) - (\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2} - 0) \\\\\n&= \\sqrt{2} - \\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2} - 1 \\\\\n&= \\frac{2\\sqrt{2} - \\sqrt{2}}{2} - 1 \\\\\n&= \\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2} - 1\n\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534405 false] [17592186114953 1145 "Splitting up the integral into the difference of two integrals and evaluating each integral separately, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /4}(\\operatorname{sec}⁡x\\operatorname{tan}⁡x-\\operatorname{cos}⁡x)\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /4}\\operatorname{sec}⁡x\\operatorname{tan}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x-{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /4}\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\operatorname{sec}⁡x\\,{|}_{0}^{\\pi /4}-\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\,{|}_{0}^{\\pi /4} \\\\  & =(\\operatorname{sec}⁡\\frac{\\pi }{4}-\\operatorname{sec}⁡0)-(\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\frac{\\pi }{4}-\\operatorname{sin}⁡0) \\\\  & =(\\sqrt{2}-1)-(\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}-0) \\\\  & =\\sqrt{2}-\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}-1 \\\\  & =\\frac{2\\sqrt{2}-\\sqrt{2}}{2}-1 \\\\  & =\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}-1.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534405 true] [17592186114958 1100 "Evaluate $\\displaystyle \\int_{-2}^2(2x^3 - 5)\\, \\textrm d x$." 13194139534405 false] [17592186114958 1100 "Evaluate $\\displaystyle \\int_{-2}^2(2x^3 - 5)\\, \\textrm d x.$" 13194139534405 true] [17592186114958 1145 "Splitting up the sum and factoring out the constants, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\int_{-2}^{2}(2x^{3} - 5)dx &= 2\\int_{-2}^{2}x^{3}dx - 5\\int_{-2}^{2}1dx \\\\\n&= 2 \\cdot \\left.\\frac{x^{4}}{4}\\right|_{-2}^{2} - \\left.5x\\right|_{-2}^{2} \\\\\n&= \\left.\\frac{1}{2}x^{4}\\right|_{-2}^{2} - \\left.5x\\right|_{-2}^{2} \\\\\n&= \\frac{1}{2}(2^{4} - (-2)^{4}) - 5(2 - (-2)) \\\\\n&= \\frac{1}{2}(16 - 16) - 5 \\cdot 4 \\\\\n&=-20\n\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534405 false] [17592186114958 1145 "Splitting up the sum and factoring out the constants, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{-2}^{2}(2{x}^{3}-5)\\,\\text{d}x & =2{\\int }_{-2}^{2}{x}^{3}\\,\\text{d}x-5{\\int }_{-2}^{2}1\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =2\\cdot \\frac{{x}^{4}}{4}{|}_{-2}^{2}-5x{|}_{-2}^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}{x}^{4}\\,{|}_{-2}^{2}-5x\\,{|}_{-2}^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}({2}^{4}-(-2)^{4})-5(2-(-2)) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}(16-16)-5\\cdot 4 \\\\  & =-20.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534405 true] [17592186114964 1100 "Calculate $\\displaystyle \\int_{1}^{4} \\left(\\sqrt x - \\dfrac 2 {x^2}\\right) \\, \\textrm d x .$" 13194139534405 true] [17592186114964 1100 "Calculate $\\displaystyle \\int_{1}^{4} \\left(\\sqrt x - \\dfrac 2 {x^2}\\right) \\, \\textrm d x$." 13194139534405 false] [17592186114964 1145 "First, we rewrite the integral as\n\n$$\n\\int_1^4 \\left( \\sqrt x - \\dfrac 2 {x^2} \\right) \\, \\textrm dx = \\int_1^4 \\left( x^{1/2}-2x^{-2} \\right) \\, \\textrm dx.\n$$\n\n \n\nThen, we split the integral into the difference of two integrals and factor out the constants. We get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{1}^{4}(\\sqrt{x}-\\frac{2}{{x}^{2}})\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{1}^{4}{x}^{1/2}\\,\\text{d}x-2{\\int }_{1}^{4}{x}^{-2}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{3}{x}^{3/2}\\,{|}_{1}^{4}+2{x}^{-1}\\,{|}_{1}^{4} \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{3}({4}^{3/2}-{1}^{3/2})+2({4}^{-1}-{1}^{-1}) \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{3}(8-1)+2(\\frac{1}{4}-1) \\\\  & =\\frac{14}{3}+2\\cdot (-\\frac{3}{4}) \\\\  & =\\frac{14}{3}-\\frac{3}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{19}{6}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534405 true] [17592186114964 1145 "First, we rewrite the integral as\n\n$$\n\\int_1^4 \\left(\\sqrt x - \\dfrac 2 {x^2} \\right) \\, \\textrm dx = \\int_1^4 \\left(x^{1/2}-2x^{-2} \\right) \\, \\textrm dx\n$$\n\nThen, we split the integral into the difference of two integrals and factor out the constants. We get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\int_{1}^{4}(\\sqrt{x} - \\frac{2}{x^{2}})dx &= \\int_{1}^{4}x^{1/2}dx - 2\\int_{1}^{4}x^{-2}dx \\\\\n&= \\left.\\frac{2}{3}x^{3/2}\\right|_{1}^{4} + \\left.2x^{-1}\\right|_{1}^{4} \\\\\n&= \\frac{2}{3}(4^{3/2} - 1^{3/2}) + 2(4^{-1} - 1^{-1}) \\\\\n&= \\frac{2}{3}(8 - 1) + 2(\\frac{1}{4} - 1) \\\\\n&= \\frac{14}{3} + 2 \\cdot (-\\frac{3}{4}) \\\\\n&= \\frac{14}{3} - \\frac{3}{2} \\\\\n&= \\frac{19}{6}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534405 false] [17592186115126 1020 #edb/ref 17592186286578 13194139534405 true] [17592186115126 1020 #edb/ref 17592186286585 13194139534405 true] [17592186115126 1020 #edb/ref 17592186286638 13194139534405 true] [17592186115126 1020 #edb/ref 17592186286642 13194139534405 true] [17592186115126 1020 #edb/ref 17592186286645 13194139534405 true] [17592186115127 1020 #edb/ref 17592186286592 13194139534405 true] [17592186115127 1020 #edb/ref 17592186286634 13194139534405 true] [17592186115127 1020 #edb/ref 17592186286648 13194139534405 true] [17592186115127 1020 #edb/ref 17592186286652 13194139534405 true] [17592186115127 1020 #edb/ref 17592186286669 13194139534405 true] [17592186115128 1020 #edb/ref 17592186286599 13194139534405 true] [17592186115128 1020 #edb/ref 17592186286606 13194139534405 true] [17592186115128 1020 #edb/ref 17592186286620 13194139534405 true] [17592186115128 1020 #edb/ref 17592186286655 13194139534405 true] [17592186115128 1020 #edb/ref 17592186286659 13194139534405 true] [17592186115129 1020 #edb/ref 17592186286613 13194139534405 true] [17592186115129 1020 #edb/ref 17592186286627 13194139534405 true] [17592186115129 1020 #edb/ref 17592186286662 13194139534405 true] [17592186115129 1020 #edb/ref 17592186286665 13194139534405 true] [17592186115638 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139534405 true] [17592186115638 1100 "${\\int }_{1}^{16}(\\frac{10}{\\sqrt[4]{{x}^{3}}}+\\frac{x}{10})\\,\\text{d}x=$" 13194139534405 true] [17592186115638 1100 "What is $\\displaystyle \\int_{1}^{16}(\\frac{10}{\\sqrt[4]{x^{3}}} + \\frac{x}{10})dx$?" 13194139534405 false] [17592186115638 1145 "First, we rewrite the integral as\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{1}^{16}(\\frac{10}{\\sqrt[4]{{x}^{3}}}+\\frac{x}{10})\\,\\text{d}x={\\int }_{1}^{16}(10{x}^{-3/4}+\\frac{1}{10}x)\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nThen, we split the integral into the difference of two integrals and factor out the constants. We get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{1}^{16}(10{x}^{-3/4}+\\frac{1}{10}x)\\,\\text{d}x & =10{\\int }_{1}^{16}{x}^{-3/4}\\,\\text{d}x+\\frac{1}{10}{\\int }_{1}^{16}x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =10\\cdot 4{x}^{1/4}\\,{|}_{1}^{16}+\\frac{1}{10}\\cdot \\frac{{x}^{2}}{2}\\,{|}_{1}^{16} \\\\  & =40{x}^{1/4}\\,{|}_{1}^{16}+\\frac{1}{20}{x}^{2}\\,{|}_{1}^{16} \\\\  & =40({16}^{1/4}-{1}^{1/4})+\\frac{1}{20}({16}^{2}-{1}^{2}) \\\\  & =40(2-1)+\\frac{1}{20}(256-1) \\\\  & =40+\\frac{51}{4} \\\\  & =\\frac{211}{4}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534405 true] [17592186286578 1017 #edb/ref 17592186286579 13194139534405 true] [17592186286578 1089 "q-114168" 13194139534405 true] [17592186286578 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139534405 true] [17592186286578 1100 "${\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}(-3\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta )\\,\\text{d}\\theta =$" 13194139534405 true] [17592186286578 1113 #uuid "b6fd042a-ba9e-5baa-b53c-650b162950c7" 13194139534405 true] [17592186286578 1145 "Factoring the constant out of the integral, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}(-3\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta )\\,\\text{d}\\theta  & =-3{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta \\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & =-3(-\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta )\\,{|}_{0}^{\\pi /2} \\\\  & =3(\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta )\\,{|}_{0}^{\\pi /2} \\\\  & =3[\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{2})-\\operatorname{cos}⁡0] \\\\  & =3(0-1) \\\\  & =-3.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534405 true] [17592186286579 1000 #edb/ref 17592186286580 13194139534405 true] [17592186286579 1000 #edb/ref 17592186286581 13194139534405 true] [17592186286579 1000 #edb/ref 17592186286582 13194139534405 true] [17592186286579 1000 #edb/ref 17592186286583 13194139534405 true] [17592186286579 1000 #edb/ref 17592186286584 13194139534405 true] [17592186286579 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139534405 true] [17592186286579 1041 "selection" 13194139534405 true] [17592186286579 1104 #edb/ref 17592186286583 13194139534405 true] [17592186286579 1110 #uuid "9a1a3e64-8155-52b6-9416-3b5333f40451" 13194139534405 true]